<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Archive and its editorial principles." language="en" alternateLanguageUrl="/about/">
  <article class="prose-page shell">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About this publication</p>
      <h1>A working archive for ideas that deserve a longer life.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <aside><p>Investing</p><p>AI & AX</p><p>Coding</p><p>Mathematics</p><p>Misc</p></aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lead">The Archive is an independent research and knowledge publication by Jacob Shin.</p>
        <p>Its Korean articles begin with a topic brief, essential claims, and a logical structure. English editions are then edited from the same argument and evidence rather than translated mechanically.</p>
        <h2>Editorial method</h2>
        <p><strong>Explain → Model → Test → Interpret.</strong> Prefer primary sources, distinguish evidence from inference, and expose the model, code, or calculation when it matters.</p>
        <h2>Corrections and investment disclaimer</h2>
        <p>Material changes are reflected in the updated date. Investing articles are for research and education only and are not investment advice or recommendations.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
